## Bug fixes
- **Reflections dropped out, or counted twice, where a façade has a vertex a few centimetres off straight.** Footprints traced from maps often split one straight wall into several pieces with a slight bend between them. Each piece was treated as a separate reflector, so:
  - at an outward bend, neither piece reflected over a thin strip, which showed as needles or hairy spikes in contours (5.5 dB deep on a P2006 section);
  - at an inward bend, both pieces reflected, counting the same reflection twice;
  - each short piece was tested against the reflector-size rule (ISO 9613-2 Formula 26) on its own, so a wall could be ignored because it was drawn in pieces.

  A wall that stays within 4 cm of flat now reflects as one wall. Screening still uses the exact footprint, and a wall is never joined across a point where a neighbouring building touches it. Of 290 receptors in 28 test projects, only the 3 on P2006 changed (by 1 to 5.5 dB, where a façade drawn in pieces now passes the size rule). Recalculate projects with reflections switched on.
